# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

A Soroban NFT contract scaffolded by [Sorobix](https://github.com/Soro-Bix/soroban-scaffold).

## Template: NFT (Non-Fungible Token)

A non-fungible token contract with per-token ownership, metadata URIs, and an
approval mechanism for delegated transfers.

- Unique `u64` token IDs
- Per-token metadata URI (`ipfs://…`, `https://…`, or anything else)
- Owner-gated transfer and burn
- Single-token approvals with `approve` / `transfer_from`
- Events published on mint, transfer, approve, and burn
- `require_auth()` on every state-changing function

## Prerequisites

- Rust 1.76+ with the `wasm32-unknown-unknown` target
- [Stellar CLI](https://developers.stellar.org/docs/build/smart-contracts/setup)

## Build

```bash
cargo build --target wasm32-unknown-unknown --release
```

The optimized WASM will be at:

```
target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/{{PROJECT_NAME}}.wasm
```

## Test

```bash
cargo test --locked
```

13 tests cover the full lifecycle: initialization, minting, duplicate-ID
rejection, transfers, approvals, delegated transfers, burning, and the
unauthorized path for each.

## Contract API

### Administration

| Function | Description |
|---|---|
| `initialize(admin, name, symbol)` | Sets the collection admin and metadata. Callable once. |

### Minting and burning

| Function | Description |
|---|---|
| `mint(admin, to, token_id, metadata_uri)` | Admin-only. Fails if `token_id` already exists. |
| `burn(owner, token_id)` | Owner-only. Destroys the token and decrements supply. |

### Transfers

| Function | Description |
|---|---|
| `transfer(from, to, token_id)` | Owner-only direct transfer. |
| `approve(owner, spender, token_id)` | Authorizes `spender` to move one specific token. |
| `transfer_from(spender, from, to, token_id)` | Transfer performed by an approved spender. |

### Views

| Function | Returns |
|---|---|
| `owner_of(token_id)` | Current owner, or `TokenNotFound` |
| `token_uri(token_id)` | Metadata URI, or `TokenNotFound` |
| `get_approved(token_id)` | Approved spender, if any |
| `balance_of(owner)` | Number of tokens held |
| `total_supply()` | Tokens currently in circulation |
| `name()` / `symbol()` | Collection metadata |

## Errors

| Error | Raised when |
|---|---|
| `AlreadyInitialized` | `initialize` called twice |
| `NotInitialized` | Any operation before `initialize` |
| `TokenAlreadyExists` | Minting a `token_id` that is already taken |
| `TokenNotFound` | Referencing a token that was never minted or has been burned |
| `NotOwner` | Caller does not own the token they are acting on |
| `NotApproved` | `transfer_from` without a matching approval |
| `Unauthorized` | Non-admin attempting to mint |

## A note on approvals

Approvals are cleared whenever a token changes hands, via either `transfer` or
`transfer_from`. Without this, a spender approved by a previous owner would
retain the ability to move the token out from under its new owner. There is a
test asserting this specific behaviour.

## Deploy (Testnet)

```bash
stellar contract deploy \
  --wasm target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/{{PROJECT_NAME}}.wasm \
  --source-account <YOUR_SECRET_KEY> \
  --rpc-url https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org:443 \
  --network-passphrase "Test SDF Network ; September 2015"
```

## Next Steps

1. Run `cargo test --locked` to confirm everything passes
2. Decide how `token_id` values are allocated for your collection
3. Consider whether you need collection-wide operator approval
   (`set_approval_for_all`) in addition to per-token approvals
4. Point `metadata_uri` at your real metadata host

